From 41a672e0dbd376d5047ebbd52caa664c05d1001c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <agent@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:47:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add second Unit batch data planes

Add controller-visible models for the first six Units of the second
research batch:

- joystick (U024, 0x52): controlled by the existing CONTROL_JOYSTICK
  register/snapshot path (3 bytes at 0x52); same protocol as joystick-v11 and
  the 0x52 address conflict stays documented. No new kind.
- watering (U101): dual-endpoint GPIO model. The white wire is sampled by the
  existing ADC controller hook and exposed as analog-mv/adc-samples; the yellow
  PUMP_EN pad gets an output listener and reset listener so pump-level and
  pump-transitions observe real guest pad writes instead of faking a GPIO
  return value. Pump/soil physics is NOT modeled.
- fader (U123): dual-endpoint GPIO model with white ADC sampling plus the
  existing RMT capture path configured for 14 SK6812 LEDs (led-rgb,
  led-frames, incomplete-frames). The frame bytes are whatever the frozen
  driver sends; palette/mechanics are NOT modeled and the neopixel snapshot vs
  master set_brightness difference is documented.
- dac (U012, MCP4725 0x60): bare-command slave (no register pointer). Fast-mode
  writes update the 12-bit register; 0x60||value commands commit DAC+EEPROM;
  reads return the official 3-byte [ready-status, value>>4, (value&0xf)<<4]
  shape. QOM dac-raw/dac-voltage-v/eeprom-value/eeprom-writes; the voltage
  fixture uses the driver's default vdd=5.0 V and the physical 0..3.3 V range
  stays UNRESOLVED.
- bps (U090, BMP280 0x76): chip id 0x58, reset/status/control/config
  registers, fixed synthetic-but-valid 24-byte calibration block and 0xF7
  data registers derived by inverting the executable driver's integer
  compensation (floor division preserved) so the guest's own compensation
  reproduces temperature-c/pressure-pa. QMP6988 fallback (0x56/0x70) is NOT
  modeled.
- adc-v11 (0x48, ADS1110): single-byte config, 2-byte big-endian signed reads;
  the raw count is derived from voltage-mv with the official ADS1110
  mini-code/gain/divider formula. The page's ADS1100/rate/reference
  contradictions stay UNRESOLVED.

All six are transaction/controller models only; registers/addresses follow the
executable drivers or official tables, and no runtime profile is upgraded
without guest evidence.
---
